Frequently Asked Questions
Does ceramic coating really protect against scratches? Ceramic coating adds hardness that helps reduce light swirl marks, but it doesn't make your car scratch-proof. Deeper scratches from keys or branches can still happen.
Do I still need to wash my car after ceramic coating? Yes, regular washing is still necessary after ceramic coating. The coating just makes dirt and grime easier to rinse away during each wash.
How long does ceramic coating actually last? Ceramic coating typically lasts 1 to 2 years for consumer-grade products, while professional-grade coatings can last 3 to 5 years or more. Proper maintenance plays a big role in how long it holds up.
Is spray-on ceramic coating the same as professional application? No, spray-on ceramic products offer lighter, shorter-term protection compared to professionally applied coatings. Professional application involves paint prep and multiple bonded layers for better results.
What are the main benefits of ceramic coating for cars? Ceramic coating adds a glossy finish while also protecting against UV rays, oxidation, and stains. It also makes ongoing maintenance and washing noticeably easier.
Is ceramic coating worth the investment? Ceramic coating is generally worth it for drivers who want long-term paint protection and easier upkeep. It works best when paired with realistic expectations and proper care afterward.
